      "description": "Horizontal preview of icon-and-label navigation; bottom navigation stacks icons and rail aligns rows.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-nav\" aria-label=\"Squirrel destinations\"><button class=\"ds-tab\" aria-current=\"page\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3H10V10H3ZM14 3H21V10H14ZM3 14H10V21H3ZM14 14H21V21H14Z\"/></svg>Connection</button><button class=\"ds-tab\">Proxies</button><button class=\"ds-tab\">Configuration</button></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{display:flex;gap:4px;padding:6px 12px;background:#FCFCFD;overflow-x:auto}.ds-tab{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;min-height:48px;padding:8px 12px;border:0;border-radius:8px;background:transparent;color:#666E80;font:400 13px sans-serif;cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap}.ds-tab[aria-current]{background:#EDF0FD;color:#5366CA;font-weight:700}.ds-tab svg{width:18px;height:18px;fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.6}.ds-tab:hover{cursor:pointer}.ds-tab:active{background-image:linear-gradient(#E3E7EF66,#E3E7EF66)}.ds-tab:focus-visible{outline:auto}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.ds-nav{background:#191C24}.ds-tab{color:#A2A9B9}.ds-tab[aria-current]{background:#2C3350;color:#98A8FF}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Selection chip",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "route-chip",
      "description": "Textual outbound selection state; it is not an independent action.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-chip\">Selected · relay-a</span>",
      "css": ".ds-chip{display:block;font:700 13px sans-serif;background:#EDF0FD;color:#5366CA;border-radius:8px;padding:7px 10px}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.ds-chip{background:#2C3350;color:#98A8FF}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Status panel",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "panel",
      "description": "Shared outlined panel. Compact Connection omits the panel heading and moves its primary action ahead of wrapping detail/profile.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-panel\"><h2 class=\"ds-panel-title\">Network status</h2><strong class=\"ds-state\">Disconnected</strong><p class=\"ds-detail\">Ready when you are</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{font:400 14px sans-serif;color:#292E3D;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #E3E7EF;border-radius:12px;padding:16px;box-shadow:none}.ds-panel-title{font-size:15px;font-weight:700;margin:0 0 16px}.ds-state{font-size:20px}.ds-detail{font-size:13px;color:#666E80;margin:4px 0 0}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.ds-panel{background:#1C2029;color:#E3E7F1;border-color:#2C3240}.ds-detail{color:#A2A9B9}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Paired transfer tiles",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "panel",
      "description": "Downloaded first with periwinkle icon; uploaded second with teal icon. Slate figures use 24sp tabular totals. No sample traffic is implied.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-pair\"><section class=\"ds-tile\"><span class=\"ds-label\"><svg class=\"ds-down\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M7 7V17H17M7 17L19 5\"/></svg>Downloaded</span><strong class=\"ds-total\">—</strong><small>Total downloaded</small></section><section class=\"ds-tile\"><span class=\"ds-label\"><svg class=\"ds-up\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M7 7H17V17M17 7L5 19\"/></svg>Uploaded</span><strong class=\"ds-total\">—</strong><small>Total uploaded</small></section></div>",
      "css": ".ds-pair{display:flex;gap:12px;font-family:sans-serif}.ds-tile{flex:1;min-width:0;padding:16px;border:1px solid #E3E7EF;border-radius:12px;background:#FFFFFF;color:#292E3D}.ds-label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;color:#666E80;font-size:12px;margin-bottom:12px}.ds-label svg{width:18px;height:18px;stroke-width:1.6;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;fill:none}.ds-down{stroke:#5366CA}.ds-up{stroke:#237F77}.ds-total{display:block;font-size:24px;font-weight:700;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.ds-tile small{display:block;font-size:11px;color:#666E80;margin-top:8px}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.ds-tile{background:#1C2029;color:#E3E7F1;border-color:#2C3240}.ds-label,.ds-tile small{color:#A2A9B9}.ds-down{stroke:#98A8FF}.ds-up{stroke:#65CBBD}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Engine metric row",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "panel",
      "description": "Label/value alignment within the engine panel; divider is 1dp and value uses tabular figures.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-engine\"><span>Resident memory</span><strong>—</strong></div>",
      "css": ".ds-engine{display:flex;align-items:center;border-bottom:1px solid #E3E7EF;background:#FFFFFF;color:#666E80;font:400 14px sans-serif}.ds-engine span{flex:1;padding:13px 12px 13px 0}.ds-engine strong{flex:1.4;color:#292E3D;text-align:right;padding:13px 0;font-weight:700;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.ds-engine{background:#1C2029;color:#A2A9B9;border-color:#2C3240}.ds-engine strong{color:#E3E7F1}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "YAML editor",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "yaml-editor",
      "description": "Native source pane with 1dp resting and 2dp focused stroke. Browser line metrics approximate native metrics plus 2dp; no IME reproduction.",
      "html": "<textarea class=\"ds-yaml\" aria-label=\"YAML configuration editor\" wrap=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\"># Synthetic documentation preview\noutbounds: []</textarea>",
      "css": ".ds-yaml{display:block;max-width:100%;min-height:180px;font:400 13px monospace;line-height:calc(1.2em + 2px);color:#292E3D;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #E3E7EF;border-radius:12px;padding:14px;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;resize:vertical}.ds-yaml:hover{border-color:#E3E7EF}.ds-yaml:focus,.ds-yaml:focus-visible{border:2px solid #5366CA;outline:none}.ds-yaml::selection{background:#5366CA33}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.ds-yaml{background:#1C2029;color:#E3E7F1;border-color:#2C3240}.ds-yaml:focus,.ds-yaml:focus-visible{border-color:#98A8FF}.ds-yaml::selection{background:#98A8FF33}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Selectable output",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "log-viewer",
      "description": "Logs and API protocol/JSON results reuse this source role. Log export remains independent of live/filter display. Browser line metrics approximate native metrics plus 3dp.",
      "html": "<pre class=\"ds-output\" tabindex=\"0\">— service.log —\nINFO Synthetic documentation preview</pre>",
      "css": ".ds-output{font:400 12px monospace;line-height:calc(1.2em + 3px);color:#292E3D;background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #E3E7EF;border-radius:12px;padding:14px;white-space:pre-wrap;max-height:180px;overflow:auto;user-select:text}.ds-output:focus-visible{outline:auto}.ds-output::selection{background:#5366CA33}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.ds-output{background:#1C2029;color:#E3E7F1;border-color:#2C3240}.ds-output::selection{background:#98A8FF33}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Squirrelboard native dashboard",
    "overview": "Squirrelboard’s precise dashboard language expressed through native Android Views. A cool gray canvas supports white outlined panels, slate text, periwinkle selection and teal transfer accents. Charcoal day/night counterparts preserve the same hierarchy. The local reference is `../squirrelboard`; the native implementation owns the values recorded here, including stronger light-mode text accents for contrast.\n\nThe same materials cover Connection, Proxies, Configuration, Logs, Sessions, API tools and app-owned dialogs. Technical detail remains visible through labeled measurements, native text scaling and large source panes. The reference squirrel mark is retained as a native vector. Android system sans replaces the reference’s web font, while YAML, logs and protocol/JSON results use native monospace.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cool gray canvas, white or charcoal panels and thin outlines.",
      "Periwinkle selection and download roles; teal upload and green local-engine status.",
      "Small rounded actions, larger panel corners and flat native ripple feedback.",
      "System sans, tabular measurements and monospace source data.",
      "Adaptive bottom navigation, horizontal tabs and an expanded navigation rail."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Labeled Direction Rule",
        "body": "Use periwinkle for download and teal for upload, and retain the direction words. Connection tiles show Downloaded then Uploaded; row pairs show Upload then Download. Color never replaces the label.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Figures Stay Put Rule",
        "body": "Use tabular figures for changing measurements and preserve identity and alignment during refresh.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Outlined Panel Rule",
        "body": "Separate work areas with panel fill and a thin outline; keep ordinary panels and actions flat.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use the matched day/night resource roles across all five destinations, API tools and app-owned dialogs.",
      "**Do** retain direction labels, tabular numbers and explicit unavailable, empty, error and busy states.",
      "**Do** use native sp scaling, dp geometry and at least 48dp for action and filter touch targets.",
      "**Do** keep Connection’s primary action before wrapping detail/profile text in short viewports.",
      "**Do** preserve long identifiers, filter state, editor drafts, secure-window behavior and live reading position.",
      "**Do** distinguish local-engine state from remote reachability, saved configuration from drafts and visible log filtering from full retained-log export."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don’t** restore violet chrome, lavender-filled workspaces or capsule actions from the superseded Technical atlas.",
      "**Don’t** shrink native controls to the reference website’s compact desktop dimensions.",
      "**Don’t** invent chart data, traffic history, remote connectivity claims or production fixture labels.",
      "**Don’t** apply the YAML focus border to every native field or replace native errors, selection and keyboard behavior.",
      "**Don’t** add shadows or web hover motion to ordinary native panels and buttons."
    ]
  }
}
